[
    {
        "content": "<p>We have a whole zoo of definitions of compositions for bundled maps: <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearMap.comp#doc\">docs#LinearMap.comp</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ContinuousLinearMap.comp#doc\">docs#ContinuousLinearMap.comp</a>, etc . They all have the same property that <code>f.comp g x = f (g x)</code> (or equivalently, <code>f.comp g</code> coerces to <code>Function.comp f g</code>). I have recently put some effort into introducing type classes that get rid of boilerplate related to algebraic operations and function application, see <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39639\">#39639</a>. I think there is a great deal of boilerplate that involves composition and algebraic operations, see for example <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearMap.comp_neg#doc\">docs#LinearMap.comp_neg</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearMap.sub_comp#doc\">docs#LinearMap.sub_comp</a>, etc (a rough estimate would be that there are 12 of these theorems per definition). So my proposal to fix this is to introduce a notation typeclass for composition (with nice notation) and remove all of the manual <code>comp</code> definitions in favour of implementing an instance of this typeclass.</p>",
        "id": 601756597,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1781091477
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sounds good. Do you have a quasi-formal sketch of what that would look like?</p>",
        "id": 601836142,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1781106312
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm a bit concerned about performance and/or elaboration (i.e., I think we have <code>∘L</code> for this reason), but I would be still be interested in seeing a PR.</p>",
        "id": 601836906,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1781106456
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Would we want to be able to use <code>∘</code> notation for this if it were possible to write an appropriate elaborator?</p>",
        "id": 601842844,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781107514
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would suggest not. It's useful to be able to get into function world using <code>⇑</code> or <code>∘</code>. And I think lots of people (e.g., downstream repos) would rightfully complain about such a feature.</p>",
        "id": 601892274,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1781117630
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So, what would be an appropriate notation for this composition?</p>",
        "id": 601892812,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781117766
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe: <code>∘ₘ</code> (<code>ₘ</code> for <em>morphism</em>), or <code>∘ᶠ</code> (<code>ᶠ</code> for <code>FunLike</code>). There's also <code>◎</code> (BULLSEYE U+25CE), but I don't like that much.</p>",
        "id": 601893617,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1781117964
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So if I understand correctly, this is the class we are considering, right?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CompLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outParam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FunLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FunLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FunLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">coe_comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⇑</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⇑</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⇑</span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>With some notation for <code>CompLike.comp</code>.</p>",
        "id": 601897482,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781118919
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>HasComp</code>?</p>",
        "id": 601897540,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1781118936
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I didn't really think about the name yet. Though I thought we were phasing out the <code>Has</code> naming convention for notation type classes.</p>",
        "id": 601898033,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781119050
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>FWIW we still have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Function.HasUncurry#doc\">docs#Function.HasUncurry</a> but maybe we want to rename it?<br>\nWe also have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=HasQuotient#doc\">docs#HasQuotient</a> because <code>Quotient</code> is taken, and core has <code>HasSubset</code>/<code>HasSSubset</code> but somehow also <code>Superset</code>/<code>SSuperset</code>.<br>\nSo <code>Comp</code> sounds good</p>",
        "id": 601900843,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1781119701
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, probably it should be renamed to <code>Function.Uncurry</code>.</p>",
        "id": 601901631,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781119886
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I wonder if <code>Comp.comp</code> could be confused with <code>Function.comp</code>.</p>",
        "id": 601901894,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781119949
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479299\">Jovan Gerbscheid</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/RFC.3A.20notation.20typeclass.20for.20composition/near/601897482\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So if I understand correctly, this is the class we are considering, right?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CompLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outParam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FunLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FunLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FunLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">coe_comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⇑</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⇑</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⇑</span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>With some notation for <code>CompLike.comp</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think it might be more consistent with the rest of the classes if it was split into two classes</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outParam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsCompApply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outParam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FunLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FunLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FunLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">comp_apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I think that this would also be better for finding instances, because every <code>Comp</code> should get implemented directly by every class, so typeclass search should be really quick to either succeed or fail</p>",
        "id": 601954912,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1781134365
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I haven't thought about notation too much, Jireh's suggestions both sound good to me</p>",
        "id": 601956118,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1781134833
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe we could \"steal\" <code>∘'</code> from <code>Function.dcomp</code> (and add an instance for dependent functions so that it would keep working)</p>",
        "id": 601957009,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1781135143
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The function could also be called <code>Comp.fcomp</code> or <code>Comp.mcomp</code> (depending on the notation) if we are afraid that otherwise it would clash with <code>Function.comp</code> (I am not too worried, because neither would live in the root namespace and you would probably never open <code>Comp</code>).</p>",
        "id": 601957041,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1781135153
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another issue is that of naming. Calling it <code>fcomp</code> or <code>mcomp</code> could help distinguish it from usual composition.</p>",
        "id": 601957208,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781135220
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ContinuousLinearMap.comp#doc\">docs#ContinuousLinearMap.comp</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearMap.comp#doc\">docs#LinearMap.comp</a> is a thing currently..</p>",
        "id": 601957485,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1781135322
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>calling it <code>Comp.comp</code> would result in less deprecations</p>",
        "id": 601957665,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1781135387
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Although 46 equiv types would still take the hit<br>\n<a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/id.2Fcomp.20vs.20refl.2Ftrans.20for.20embeddings.20and.20equivs/near/593162942\">#mathlib4 &gt; id/comp vs refl/trans for embeddings and equivs @ 💬</a></p>",
        "id": 601958061,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1781135537
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh no, now I'm thinking we should use <code>One</code> instances to replace all the <code>id</code> defs <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 601958706,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1781135775
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/RFC.3A.20notation.20typeclass.20for.20composition/near/601958706\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Oh no, now I'm thinking we should use <code>One</code> instances to replace all the <code>id</code> defs <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I thought about that and it only has the problem that you wouldn't be able to write <code>.id R M</code> for <code>LinearMap.id R M</code>, but <code>1 : M →ₗ[R] M</code></p>",
        "id": 601959145,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1781135941
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think ultimately I want to get rid of all of the definitions that are not specific to a type like <code>.comp</code>, <code>.id</code>, etc. There are so much issues with consistency and you can't outsource the boilerplate really if they are their own definitions without a general typeclass.<br>\nImagine if each type had their own <code>.add</code>, <code>.sub</code>, etc. with their own notation for addition of (continuous) linear maps. I don't see a fundamental difference between that and <code>.comp</code> and <code>.id</code> (or <code>.trans</code> and <code>.refl</code> and <code>.symm</code>).</p>",
        "id": 601960779,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1781136266
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/RFC.3A.20notation.20typeclass.20for.20composition/near/601958706\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Oh no, now I'm thinking we should use <code>One</code> instances to replace all the <code>id</code> defs <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This doesn't work for MonoidHom, where <code>1</code> is the constant map and <code>id</code> is the identity</p>",
        "id": 601973743,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781139345
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also for <code>OneHom</code> and <code>MulHom</code>, but <code>1</code> in <code>Monoid.End</code> is the identity, that's so strange<br>\nI wonder if people use these (it also has <code>Mul</code> for composition).<br>\nIn any case, we could use <code>𝟙</code> (<code>\\b1</code>) like categories, or <code>𝟏</code> (U+1D7CF)</p>",
        "id": 601978152,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1781140815
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Or, hear me out, <span aria-label=\"id\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f194\" role=\"img\" title=\"id\">:id:</span> (U+1F194)</p>",
        "id": 601978436,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1781140923
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(probably a can of worm) should the new typeclass also cover <code>*Equiv.trans</code>?</p>",
        "id": 601978947,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1781141100
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it would cover <code>*Equiv.trans</code>, simply by strengthening the assumption from <code>FunLike</code> to <code>EquivLike</code>.</p>",
        "id": 601983127,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781142597
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sure, but the convention for the notation is backwards? (<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Equiv.coe_trans#doc\">docs#Equiv.coe_trans</a> flips the order)</p>",
        "id": 601983198,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781142621
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So let's choose one order and stick to it!</p>",
        "id": 601983304,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781142672
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Watch out, you'll invent category theory soon</p>",
        "id": 601988553,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781144557
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/RFC.3A.20notation.20typeclass.20for.20composition/near/601973743\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/RFC.3A.20notation.20typeclass.20for.20composition/near/601958706\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Oh no, now I'm thinking we should use <code>One</code> instances to replace all the <code>id</code> defs <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This doesn't work for MonoidHom, where <code>1</code> is the constant map and <code>id</code> is the identity</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/RFC.3A.20notation.20typeclass.20for.20composition/near/601978152\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also for <code>OneHom</code> and <code>MulHom</code>, but <code>1</code> in <code>Monoid.End</code> is the identity, that's so strange<br>\nI wonder if people use these (it also has <code>Mul</code> for composition).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40515\">#40515</a> turns <code>OrderHom</code> into a <code>Monoid</code> and <code>OrderIso</code> into a <code>Group</code>.<br>\nIs this something we want to do for most homs/equivs instead of <code>Comp</code>?</p>",
        "id": 602342170,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1781225901
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We do have it most of the time, but the composition there only works for <code>α →o α</code>, not <code>α →o β</code></p>",
        "id": 602342559,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1781226022
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Category-theoretic arrows of course go one stage further but then restrict the two ends to be in the same universe</p>",
        "id": 602350472,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781228799
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40541\">#40541</a> (<code>Topology/Algebra/Module/ContinuousLinearMap/Basic.lean</code> and <code>Algebra/Notation/Defs.lean</code> are the files to look at) I have only done a very naive search&amp;replace, and no attempts of fixing issues. Obviously the whole thing would result in more type annotations here and there.</p>",
        "id": 602486306,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1781263773
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Currently I can write something like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→ₗ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and elab knows that the underscores are <code>LinearMap</code>s, so I can use dot notation in them. Am I correct in understanding that the proposed design would lose this?</p>",
        "id": 603095810,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1781455908
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, this would indeed be a problem. It might be possible though to have a special elaborator that can help to pass the expected type through.</p>",
        "id": 603099017,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1781457142
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Potentially we could switch the existing <code>\\circ\\_l</code> notation (and similar) to be notation for the new generalized <code>Comp.comp</code>, but with some of the type arguments filled in.</p>",
        "id": 603188678,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1781489227
    }
]